  {
    "id": "frostmere_provisioner",
    "name": "Frostmere Provisioner",
    "$comment": "The equipment store canon asks for, and the only shop in Caelora where the town pays half of one line on the list. Rope is subsidised because a guide rope on every street is the reason nobody has been lost since 1849, and a public good the town buys is a cheaper policy than a search party. Everything else carries the cost of a barrel over the Wintergate, which is why the restoratives here are dear and the cold-weather goods are not. Thawcloth is the deepest stock in the game at this point on the road, for the obvious reason: this is the Frost Hall town, and the two Frost kin on the mountain both freeze what they hit.",
    "greeting": [
      "Rope is half price and the town pays the rest. The rest of it came over the pass on a sledge."
    ],
